# r_eplicate is APL's replicate (B11): one count per major cell of the
# right argument, each cell repeated that many times; a scalar count
# extends to every cell, a count of 0 drops the cell, so a mask of
# 1s and 0s (or a comparison) compresses. Rows of a matrix are its cells.
== SOURCE
1 0 2 r_eplicate "abc"
3 r_eplicate 1 2
2 r_eplicate 7
0 r_eplicate 1 2 3
(1 0 1 0 = 1) r_eplicate 10 20 30 40
(3 1 4 1 5 > 2) r_eplicate 3 1 4 1 5
2 0 1 r_eplicate 3 2 r_eshape r_ange 6
1 2 3 r_eplicate 1.5 2.5 3.5
s_hape 0 0 r_eplicate 2 3 r_eshape 0
== TYPE
Char
Int
Int
Int
Int
Int
Int
Float
Int
== RESULT
acc
1 1 1 2 2 2
7 7

10 30
3 4 5
1 2
1 2
5 6
1.5 2.5 2.5 3.5 3.5 3.5
0 3
